diagnosis of a brain tumor. The risk of seizures varies by tumor type and its location in the brain. For a long time we 
believed that preventing seizures with antiepileptic drugs (seizure prophylaxis) was effective and necessary, but the   
supporting evidence was little and mixed. Such evidence was the basis for previous reviews to conclude that seizure     
