  media-associated seizures are discussed."}, {"study_index": 15, "title": "Prophylactic anticonvulsants for            
  prevention of immediate and early postcraniotomy seizures", "abstract": "Phenytoin (15 mg/kg) was administered        
  intravenously to 189 patients shortly before their intracranial, supratentorial surgery was completed. Intravenous    
  phenytoin of 5-6 mg/kg/day in three divided doses was administered daily for the first 3 postoperative days.          
  Therapeutic serum levels (10-20 micrograms/mL) were achieved in 113 (59.8%) patients. An equally constituted,         
